353 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Today\220s preparedness indices and risk tools are useful but fragmented. Thus, we recommend building a next-generation, modular Pandemic Risk Assessment \(PRA\) framework that is dynamic, sub-nationally granular, and explicitly decision-oriented so governments and funders can translate risk into clear priorities, triggers, and investments. What we did)/E(Today\220s preparedness indices and risk tools are useful but fragmented. Thus, we recommend building a next-generation, modular Pandemic Risk Assessment \(PRA\) framework that is dynamic, sub-nationally granular, and explicitly decision-oriented so governments and funders can translate risk into clear priorities, triggers, and investments. What we did)/Pg 9 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

354 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1319 0 R/T(Conducted a scoping review of major global and national preparedness and epidemiological risk tools and the literature evaluating them, synthesizing evidence across 59 included documents.)/E(Conducted a scoping review of major global and national preparedness and epidemiological risk tools and the literature evaluating them, synthesizing evidence across 59 included documents.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

355 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1320 0 R/T(Reviewed 11 representative tools spanning preparedness benchmarking, pathogen-specific risk assessment, broader risk indices, and forecasting/modeling platforms.)/E(Reviewed 11 representative tools spanning preparedness benchmarking, pathogen-specific risk assessment, broader risk indices, and forecasting/modeling platforms.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[2 3]>>
endobj

356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1321 0 R/T(Supplemented the review with 27 anonymized expert consultations across multilateral organizations, academia, financing, nonprofits, and the private sector to identify end-user needs and barriers to uptake.)/E(Supplemented the review with 27 anonymized expert consultations across multilateral organizations, academia, financing, nonprofits, and the private sector to identify end-user needs and barriers to uptake.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

357 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(What we found Current tools are valuable but incomplete and often misunderstood or misapplied. Many preparedness indices are descriptive rather than predictive, pathogen-specific tools are narrow, and modeling platforms are not consistently translated into decision-ready outputs. Thus, no single approach provides globally integrated, actionable, and forward-looking insight across pathogen emergence, transmission dynamics, and policy levers. The most consequential gaps cluster around:)/E(What we found Current tools are valuable but incomplete and often misunderstood or misapplied. Many preparedness indices are descriptive rather than predictive, pathogen-specific tools are narrow, and modeling platforms are not consistently translated into decision-ready outputs. Thus, no single approach provides globally integrated, actionable, and forward-looking insight across pathogen emergence, transmission dynamics, and policy levers. The most consequential gaps cluster around:)/Pg 9 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

358 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1322 0 R/T(Overreliance on static variables and irregular updating, limiting timeliness and predictive value.)/E(Overreliance on static variables and irregular updating, limiting timeliness and predictive value.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

359 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1323 0 R/T(Insufficient subnational granularity, which masks local variation in risk and capacity.)/E(Insufficient subnational granularity, which masks local variation in risk and capacity.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

