364 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1325 0 R/T(Weak linkage to economic and fiscal impacts, despite these being central to fiscal policymakers and multilateral/nonprofit funder decision-making.)/E(Weak linkage to economic and fiscal impacts, despite these being central to fiscal policymakers and multilateral/nonprofit funder decision-making.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

365 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Core design principles The report distills twelve design principles for future PRA tools. These span clarity of purpose, data governance, transparency, ownership, inclusion of emerging risks, dynamic updating, uncertainty communication, subnational flexibility, and decision-use features like cost-benefit analysis and risk tiers. Recommendations for a next-generation PRA We recommend a PRA ecosystem that is modular, dynamically updated, politically and economically legible, and institutionally anchored, including:)/E(Core design principles The report distills twelve design principles for future PRA tools. These span clarity of purpose, data governance, transparency, ownership, inclusion of emerging risks, dynamic updating, uncertainty communication, subnational flexibility, and decision-use features like cost-benefit analysis and risk tiers. Recommendations for a next-generation PRA We recommend a PRA ecosystem that is modular, dynamically updated, politically and economically legible, and institutionally anchored, including:)/Pg 10 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

366 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1326 0 R/T(Mixed governance across global/regional/national actors, a clearly communicated mandate, transparent methods, and explicit uncertainty ranges.)/E(Mixed governance across global/regional/national actors, a clearly communicated mandate, transparent methods, and explicit uncertainty ranges.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

367 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1327 0 R/T(Subnational data integration plus sociopolitical signals as core determinants.)/E(Subnational data integration plus sociopolitical signals as core determinants.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

368 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1328 0 R/T(Environmental/ecological drivers as structural risk factors, real-time/automated updating, and a modular architecture linking components like spillover ecology, health-system stress, sociopolitical vulnerability, and biosafety/biosecurity.)/E(Environmental/ecological drivers as structural risk factors, real-time/automated updating, and a modular architecture linking components like spillover ecology, health-system stress, sociopolitical vulnerability, and biosafety/biosecurity.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[5]>>
