472 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(For each selected framework, we  searched for published evaluations, com- mentaries, and analyses addressing  their design, implementation, uptake,  and documented strengths and limit- ations. Databases searched included  Google Scholar, PubMed, Scopus, Web of Science Core Collection, OpenAlex, JSTOR, and Policy Commons, supplemented by targeted grey-literature searches. Search terms included the names of each framework and concepts such as \215governance,\216 \215policy uptake,\216 \215data gaps,\216 \215predictive value,\216 \215emerging risks,\216 \215climate,\216 and \215infectious disease,\216 using Boolean operators. All materials were in English and published between 1991 and 2025.)/E(For each selected framework, we  searched for published evaluations, com- mentaries, and analyses addressing  their design, implementation, uptake,  and documented strengths and limit- ations. Databases searched included  Google Scholar, PubMed, Scopus, Web of Science Core Collection, OpenAlex, JSTOR, and Policy Commons, supplemented by targeted grey-literature searches. Search terms included the names of each framework and concepts such as \215governance,\216 \215policy uptake,\216 \215data gaps,\216 \215predictive value,\216 \215emerging risks,\216 \215climate,\216 and \215infectious disease,\216 using Boolean operators. All materials were in English and published between 1991 and 2025.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

473 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(Across both stages, 59 documents met our inclusion criteria. Our team extracted key information on scope, methods, governance, outputs, reported influence, and limitations. We then conducted a thematic synthesis, organizing findings into three categories: 1\) data and governance gaps 2\) end-user engagement and output design, and 3\) emerging considerations. This scoping review informed our comparative analysis and supports the recommendations presented below.)/E(Across both stages, 59 documents met our inclusion criteria. Our team extracted key information on scope, methods, governance, outputs, reported influence, and limitations. We then conducted a thematic synthesis, organizing findings into three categories: 1\) data and governance gaps 2\) end-user engagement and output design, and 3\) emerging considerations. This scoping review informed our comparative analysis and supports the recommendations presented below.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[21 22]>>
endobj

