<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1448 0 R/E(Ambiguous Assessment Focus: Experts highlighted community confusion on what existing tools actually assess and how they differ from one another.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

723 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1449 0 R/E(Socio-political Factors: Existing tools either completely ignore socio-political factors or only cover them at a high level, which prevents proper estimation of attributed risk \(as seen during COVID-19\).)/Pg 42 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

724 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1450 0 R/E(Output Type: Existing tools possess diverse output types which have varying levels of utility in communicating a country\220s unique pandemic risk status. For example, experts consistently highlight that scorecards and rankings were not useful for making policy decisions.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

725 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1451 0 R/E(Local Context: Existing tools lack sub-national granularity, as they fail to integrate local contextual factors which affect community-level pandemic risk.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

726 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1452 0 R/E(Diversity of Needs: Current assessments do not provide customized output information for different groups of end-users with diverse needs to maximize tool utility.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[7]>>
