746 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(In this section, we outline twelve distinct design principles that a future PRA framework should follow \(Figure 2\). These principles are divided among foundational, architectural and operational, and output and use categories. They were informed by our literature review of gaps and weaknesses in existing frameworks, and by our consultations with experts who shared their experiences with and reflections from working with these tools.)/E(In this section, we outline twelve distinct design principles that a future PRA framework should follow \(Figure 2\). These principles are divided among foundational, architectural and operational, and output and use categories. They were informed by our literature review of gaps and weaknesses in existing frameworks, and by our consultations with experts who shared their experiences with and reflections from working with these tools.)/Pg 44 0 R/K[2 3]>>
endobj

747 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 310 0 R/Pg 44 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

748 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(FIGURE 2: DESIGN PRINCIPLES FOR PANDEMIC RISK ASSESSMENT TOOLS)/E(FIGURE 2: DESIGN PRINCIPLES FOR PANDEMIC RISK ASSESSMENT TOOLS)/Pg 44 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

749 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(\215From a national security strategy, it\220s not cost-effective to try and contain a pandemic within a region or within your own country. It is more sustainable and cost-effective in the long run to make sure everyone has the tools to deal with a particular disease or outbreak. [It is] really important to understand that if you want to care about your own population, you need to care about others too. Disease does not know borders.\216  - Expert Consultant)/E(\215From a national security strategy, it\220s not cost-effective to try and contain a pandemic within a region or within your own country. It is more sustainable and cost-effective in the long run to make sure everyone has the tools to deal with a particular disease or outbreak. [It is] really important to understand that if you want to care about your own population, you need to care about others too. Disease does not know borders.\216  - Expert Consultant)/Pg 44 0 R/K[5 6]>>
endobj

750 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 310 0 R/Pg 44 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

