811 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(Moving beyond general contextual factors, a future PRA must also take into account the rapidly changing global landscape. Emerging considerations, such as anthropogenic environmental change and artificial intelligence, threaten to significantly alter the contexts in which pandemics emerge and spread. Experts emphasized during our consultations that an informed, useful, and accurate tool should treat these factors as structural components of risk assessment, rather than as background context. In what follows, we provide an overview of the primary ways in which these forces reshape the pandemic landscape and offer recommendations for how they can be integrated into a future PRA framework. )/E(Moving beyond general contextual factors, a future PRA must also take into account the rapidly changing global landscape. Emerging considerations, such as anthropogenic environmental change and artificial intelligence, threaten to significantly alter the contexts in which pandemics emerge and spread. Experts emphasized during our consultations that an informed, useful, and accurate tool should treat these factors as structural components of risk assessment, rather than as background context. In what follows, we provide an overview of the primary ways in which these forces reshape the pandemic landscape and offer recommendations for how they can be integrated into a future PRA framework. )/Pg 50 0 R/K[0 1 2]>>
endobj

812 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Anthropogenic Environmental Change)/E(Anthropogenic Environmental Change)/Pg 50 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

813 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(A future PRA must incorporate continuous ecological, climatic, and anthropogenic monitoring to inform subnational risk evaluations and provide more accurate, comprehensive assessments. Failing to do so will misrepresent, and ultimately underestimate, the evolving risk landscape.)/E(A future PRA must incorporate continuous ecological, climatic, and anthropogenic monitoring to inform subnational risk evaluations and provide more accurate, comprehensive assessments. Failing to do so will misrepresent, and ultimately underestimate, the evolving risk landscape.)/Pg 50 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

