844 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 1466 0 R/T(Our literature review methodology, though structured, was still scoping in nature. Our search strategy only included publicly accessible databases and those available through institutional access. We also purposely selected sources, websites, and tools referred to us by the experts we spoke with. Thus, it is possible that we missed sources that were not publicly accessible, unpublished, confidential, internal, or non-English. We also focused largely on global tools and assessments, and the regional tools we included were focused on the United States.)/E(Our literature review methodology, though structured, was still scoping in nature. Our search strategy only included publicly accessible databases and those available through institutional access. We also purposely selected sources, websites, and tools referred to us by the experts we spoke with. Thus, it is possible that we missed sources that were not publicly accessible, unpublished, confidential, internal, or non-English. We also focused largely on global tools and assessments, and the regional tools we included were focused on the United States.)/Pg 56 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

845 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1467 0 R/T(Expert Consultation and Stakeholder Representation)/E(Expert Consultation and Stakeholder Representation)/Pg 56 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

846 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 1468 0 R/T(Similarly, in our expert consultations, we decided to focus on five key areas of stakeholders: private sector, government and policymakers, international and multilateral, academic and technical experts, and financing or donors; however, we used a scoping method for deciding which experts we reached out to for conducting our consultations. Several of the people we reached out to did not respond, so there may be nonresponse bias in the experts who chose to speak with us. Finally, we only spoke to stakeholders proficient in English, which limited our outreach to mainly Western stakeholders, excluding potential others in Africa, Asia, and Latin America. )/E(Similarly, in our expert consultations, we decided to focus on five key areas of stakeholders: private sector, government and policymakers, international and multilateral, academic and technical experts, and financing or donors; however, we used a scoping method for deciding which experts we reached out to for conducting our consultations. Several of the people we reached out to did not respond, so there may be nonresponse bias in the experts who chose to speak with us. Finally, we only spoke to stakeholders proficient in English, which limited our outreach to mainly Western stakeholders, excluding potential others in Africa, Asia, and Latin America. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

